{"chapter": "desirables", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02BU", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-more-morphisms-theorem-chow-finite-type}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{stacks-more-morphisms-section-Noetherian-valuative-criterion}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\noindent\n", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:46b1b2e2b0ce81057794485b04aaae6ebaa8b79a2d4f1bf9564e70883c282a68", "source_text": "This proves two notions of proper are the same. The first part of this is now available in the form of Chow's lemma for algebraic stacks, see More on Morphisms of Stacks, Theorem <REF_0001>. As a consequence we show that it suffices to use DVR's in checking the valuative criterion for properness for algebraic stacks in certain cases, see More on Morphisms of Stacks, Section <REF_0002>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:98d9def926fb094a53d07c5e86adf851e37d6bc704b531dd17fac20c2da65eee", "unit_id": "tag:02BU:p001"}
